# Do not hand-edit (normal PRs)

- **`CHANGELOG.md`** — python-semantic-release inserts **new** version headings on `main` above `<!-- version list -->` unless that version is already present. Do not bump `pyproject.toml` `version` in a feature PR. Polishing notes under an already-released heading (Keep a Changelog: Added / Changed / Fixed) is OK. You may pre-write the next version's notes in a release PR so the GitHub Release is not a raw commit subject. Match **1.2.0** length: one short line per bullet (see `.cursor/rules/50-changelog.mdc`).
- **`pyproject.toml` `version`** — bumped only by the release workflow / semantic-release.
- **`syncbot/requirements.txt`** — generated via `poetry export` / pre-commit hook from `pyproject.toml`.
- **Secrets** — never commit `.env`, `.env.deploy.*` with real values; only `*.example` templates belong in git.

If you must fix a release tooling bug, change config/workflows/docs — not fake “manual” version bumps in the files above.
